Z||000002||ur2biteme||01-08-2001||02:14 AM||||V6 to V6, the race should be even, maybe an edge to the mustang (he has a litre over you, although he is about 300-500 heavier)nearly even HP.  (stock, a 94-95 v6 pulls 145hp).  my v6 automatic mustang could do 0-60 in roughly 7.5-8.5 seconds if i caught it on a good day.  <P>now the GT should have a distinct advantage on you (before the swap to the 4.6 ohc).  these were the last 2 years of the 5.0.  they should be able to beat you, but you should be able to hold your own.  <P>this, of course is assuming that the guy in the 'stang knows how to drive it.  i used to be able to pull on the GT guys in my '94 v6 because it seems like in my area, no one knows how to drive them.  hell, i've hung with a v6 mustang with my duke fiero, mainly because the guy had no clue how to shift. <P>now, if this is a hypothetical question, cool.  but if this is an intended race, be careful please (sorry, my responsible half made me say it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )<P>hope it helps<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||01-08-2001||06:58 PM||||Haha, kinda reminds me of a time I raced my auto against a 96 v-6 stang.  I pulled a 1/4 mile on him after 1 mile, about 3-4 carlengths before I hit 2nd gear.  He didnt talk to me, or look at me, much the rest of the night  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But the 98 4.6 GT auto took 2 carlegnths on me, but I held with him til about 80 (end of 2nd gear).  Damn good race!<P>I say race any Stang you want, you wont get embarased too bad, hopefully!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
